FFmpeg 9.0.2, MSVC: end the coded-bitstream type loop on a NULL sentinel

cbs_type_table in libavcodec/cbs.c gets one entry per coded-bitstream type
through #ifdefs. None of the codecs SoX enables adds one, so with
--disable-everything the array is empty, a GNU extension MSVC rejects. The
table gains a NULL sentinel and CBS_FUNC(init) stops on it instead of on
FF_ARRAY_ELEMS.

--- a/libavcodec/cbs.c
+++ b/libavcodec/cbs.c
@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@
 #if CBS_VP9
     &CBS_FUNC(type_vp9),
 #endif
+    NULL,
 };
 
 av_cold int CBS_FUNC(init)(CodedBitstreamContext **ctx_ptr,
@@ -71,7 +72,7 @@
     int i;
 
     type = NULL;
-    for (i = 0; i < FF_ARRAY_ELEMS(cbs_type_table); i++) {
+    for (i = 0; cbs_type_table[i]; i++) {
         if (cbs_type_table[i]->codec_id == codec_id) {
             type = cbs_type_table[i];
             break;
